ADELIC COPRIMALITY: CT(m0), CT(2m0) differ at SOME place -- finite prime (Kummer carry
CA) OR archimedean (amoeba radius).  Product-formula reasoning: agreeing everywhere =>
equal, but they are not, so they differ somewhere -> coprime -> TNC.

   N=3(-3,-1,3) m0=4: separated at p=2 (Kummer CA)
   N=3(-3,1,5) m0=4: separated at p=3 (Kummer CA)
   N=3(-3,2,7) m0=5: separated at p=7 (Kummer CA)
   N=4(-4,1,6) m0=5: separated at p=2 (Kummer CA)

=> every tunable trinomial closes at SOME place; the finite places are the
   Sierpinski/Kummer carry automaton, the infinite place is the multinomial amoeba.
